  "labyrinthDuplicateWarning": "One letter appears twice on the path — it is shown in red.",
  "labyrinthCellSemantics": "labyrinth cell",
  "labyrinthMarkedSemantics": "marked as required on the path",
  "labyrinthTutorialStep1": "The path starts at A — the top-left corner. Tap a neighbouring cell to extend it.",
  "labyrinthTutorialStep2": "The other end is fixed at Z — the bottom-right corner. It grows towards the first one; when the two ends meet, the path closes.",
  "labyrinthTutorialStep3": "Tap a cell that isn't next to the path to add a blue mark: that letter must be on the path — like U, which occurs only once in the labyrinth. A long press (or right-click on desktop) crosses a cell out: that letter will not join the path — one of the two Y's, for instance. As soon as one of several identical letters joins the path, the rest are crossed out automatically.",
  "labyrinthTutorialStep4": "From A the path runs down to R, then turns towards Y and J.",
  "labyrinthTutorialStep5": "Through I and # the path climbs to the top row, to D and T.",
  "labyrinthTutorialStep6": "U occurs only once in the labyrinth, so it must be on the path. To its right lie the edge of the square and a crossed-out A, so the links run to 3 and K.",
  "labyrinthTutorialStep7": "From K the path descends through P and E to * and @.",
  "labyrinthTutorialStep8": "C, L, B and W carry the path left and down.",
  "labyrinthTutorialStep9": "Through G, & and F the path reaches the right edge, at S.",
  "labyrinthTutorialStep10": "H, N and $ turn the path downwards.",
  "labyrinthTutorialStep11": "The V in the bottom-left corner is enclosed on three sides — a dead end, so it cannot conduct. The other V, though, backs onto the bottom of the square and a crossed-out 3, so the links run to O and =.",
  "labyrinthTutorialStep12": "The X near the left edge is a dead end, so the other X must be on the path. M, X and Z remain — the path is closed.",
  "moduleSquarewordTitle": "Squarewords",
  "moduleSquarewordDescription": "Fill the grid so each keyword letter appears exactly once in every row, column, and both diagonals.",
  "squarewordListTitle": "Squarewords",
  "squarewordPuzzleN": "Squareword {n}",
  "squarewordResetConfirmTitle": "Reset the grid?",
  "squarewordResetConfirmBody": "All entered letters will be cleared.",
  "squarewordWinTitle": "Grid complete!",
  "squarewordWinBody": "You filled the grid with no repeats in any row, column, or diagonal.",
  "squarewordFilledCounter": "Filled: {filled} of {total}",
  "squarewordViolationWarning": "A letter repeats in a row, column, or diagonal — it is shown in red.",
  "squarewordCellSemantics": "squareword cell",
  "squarewordTutorialStep1": "The top row is the keyword: С Л Е З А. The word ЛЕС is already filled in at the center. Same rule as always: every row, every column, and both main diagonals hold each of the five letters exactly once.",
  "squarewordTutorialStep2": "From here on, every empty cell is forced by elimination — no guessing needed.",
  "squarewordTutorialStep3": "Л already appears in columns b and c, so it can't go in b1 or c1. Cell c3 sits on both diagonals at once (the center of a 5x5 grid) and already holds Л, so Л can't go in a1 or e1 either. That leaves only d1.",
  "squarewordTutorialStep4": "Column d already has З and Л. Cell d4 sits on the anti-diagonal, which already has А (at e5) — so d2 must be А, leaving С as the only letter left for d4.",
  "squarewordTutorialStep5": "In column b, С has nowhere to go on the main diagonal (С is already at a5), the anti-diagonal (С is already at d4), or row 3 (С is already at e3). Only b1 is left.",
  "squarewordTutorialStep6": "The fifth and last С goes in c2.",
  "squarewordTutorialStep7": "In the bottom row, only c1 is left for А.",
  "squarewordTutorialStep8": "That leaves only c4 in column c for З.",
  "squarewordTutorialStep9": "The two remaining А's land in a4 and b3.",
  "squarewordTutorialStep10": "In row 3, only a3 is left for З.",
  "squarewordTutorialStep11": "Everything else is now forced: Е at b4, Л at e4, З at e1, Е at a1, Е at e2, Л at a2, З at b2.",
  "squarewordTutorialStep12": "The grid is complete with zero violations — solved. Do the same in every puzzle: find the cells a letter is forced into, and follow the chain of eliminations.",
  "squarewordCyrillicNote": "Puzzle letters are always shown in Cyrillic — each keyword is its own Russian word, so there's no English alphabet to substitute.",
